From 396cd91346fac0bee6fc37dbf1e2a45847fc8fbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 09:13:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07183/11362] [outer-loop] Real-GPU re-test of
 REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-3 reflect() nudge on g50t: honest null

Re-ran scripts/outer_loop_sge_smoke_test.py (g50t, budget=46, real
gemma-4-12B-it GGUF, CUDA-pinned) to check whether the anti-stagnation
prompt nudge actually breaks the documented "wait" convergence
pattern. Prior null-run output preserved as
outer_loop_sge_smoke_test_pre_5699_3_nudge_baseline.json for an
honest before/after.

Result: still a null, max_level_reached=2, unchanged from baseline.
Confirmed the wiring works end-to-end with a real model (nudge fired,
propose-side taboo filter fired), but the router only called rank()
11 times in this budget so the nudge got exactly one chance to fire,
and that one reflect() reply failed to parse -- its advice never
propagated forward. Root cause (nudge-induced format fragility vs.
pre-existing reflect-parse fragility) is n=1 and not yet
distinguishable. Documented in ops/known-issues.md task 6 with a
concrete next step (raise reflect()'s output token budget on the
nudge-fired path, or a longer budget for n>1 comparison).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
